      "writtenOn": "2025-06-25T07:52:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That mentions\n\n```\nbecause the potential\nincompatibility with changes imported from other servers\n```\n\nWhat does this mean? Which other changes are we importing from other servers?\n\nFWIW I am quite surprised that we cannot get a change using `Change.Id changeId` :(",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 16,
        "startChar": 57,
        "endLine": 17,
        "endChar": 10
      },
      "revId": "236ee174d944ff9c38c1db4a6c5b9e2adc7978e3",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e63967bb_124fe942",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 17,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003935
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-06-25T07:58:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is a feature in upstream Gerrit that we are not using at Google.\nI don\u0027t know details about it, only that it\u0027s the reason why this method has been marked as deprecated, see commit message of that change [1]. We can still use `Change.Id changeId` and it works while it uniquely identifies a change (which is true as long as no other change with the same ID has been imported from another server). Alternatively we could remove the method deprecation.\n\n[1] https://gerrit-review.git.corp.google.com/c/gerrit/+/394440",
      "parentUuid": "882a208c_b3b72ac9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 16,
        "startChar": 57,
        "endLine": 17,
        "endChar": 10
      },
      "revId": "236ee174d944ff9c38c1db4a6c5b9e2adc7978e3",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0889717a_0ffa5255",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 17,
      "author": {
        "id": 1083225
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-06-25T08:03:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Alternatively we could remove the method deprecation\n\nHow would that work? I thought they deprecated the method due to some non Google related stuff?\n\nOr would we remove the deprecation only for us?\n\nOverall I am not sure why this CL is needed. If we can continue to use \n\n```\n  Change.Id changeId \u003d changeOperations.newChange().create();\n  ChangeApi changeApi \u003d gApi.changes().id(changeId.get());\n```\n\nnothing goes wrong for us, then do we need this CL?",
      "parentUuid": "e63967bb_124fe942",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 16,
        "startChar": 57,
        "endLine": 17,
        "endChar": 10
      },
      "revId": "236ee174d944ff9c38c1db4a6c5b9e2adc7978e3",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cdbb95b7_8cffdf80",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 17,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003935
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-06-25T08:08:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e How would that work? \n\nJust remove the @Deprecated annotation from the method. The Javadoc of this method already says that the change number is not guaranteed to unambiguously identify a change.\n\n\u003e Overall I am not sure why this CL is needed. If we can continue to use\n\nEither the method is deprecated, then we should stop using it. Or it is not deprecated then we can continue using it. \n\nContinuing using deprecated methods is bad because it results in warnings in the IDE, and then we have that many false warning, so that we can no longer see real warnings.",
      "parentUuid": "0889717a_0ffa5255",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 16,
        "startChar": 57,
        "endLine": 17,
        "endChar": 10
      },
      "revId": "236ee174d944ff9c38c1db4a6c5b9e2adc7978e3",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
