    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d4f9df9c_d2d69758",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 17,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003935
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-06-25T08:19:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, it\u0027s a bit troublesome to update all our tests and I\u0027m wondering if it\u0027s worth it. But well, at least also for us using \"\u003cproject\u003e\\~\u003cchange-number\u003e\" is the preferred change identifier as documented at [1]. It has the advantage over using \"\u003cchange-number\u003e\" that we do not need to do an index lookup to find the project for the change. So performance-wise using \"\u003cproject\u003e\\~\u003cchange-number\u003e\" is better than \"\u003cchange-number\u003e\" (which could be enough reason to deprecate \"\u003cchange-number\u003e\"). But I don\u0027t think it matters much for the tests. I\u0027m just annoyed by all those warnings... :(\n\n[1] https://gerrit-review.googlesource.com/Documentation/rest-api-changes.html#change-id",
      "parentUuid": "cd5fa68f_c1d6783b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 16,
        "startChar": 57,
        "endLine": 17,
        "endChar": 10
      },
      "revId": "236ee174d944ff9c38c1db4a6c5b9e2adc7978e3",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c85405d0_146f6808",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 17,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003935
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-06-25T08:25:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Well, what I do like is that \n\n```\n  ChangeIdentifier changeIdentifier \u003d changeOperations.newChange().createV2();\n  ChangeApi changeApi \u003d gApi.changes().id(changeIdentifier);\n```\n\nis still a little nicer than\n\n```\n  Change.Id changeId \u003d changeOperations.newChange().create();\n  ChangeApi changeApi \u003d gApi.changes().id(changeId.get());\n```\n\nsince we can use changeIdentifier directly, while for changeId we need to call .get() to get the int.",
